 "notes": [
  "Stationary barrier crossing creates minority domains at a constant rate per Hubble volume per e-fold, so the minority volume fraction per unit ln k is flat (= Lambda_1/2) and the number per Hubble volume at re-entry is ~ Lambda_1/2 per e-fold of scale. A fresh start at +v suppresses the largest scales (the first 20-45 e-folds after the patch start).",
  "The Gaussian approximation (linearised about +v) puts all opposite-sign volume on scales that exited in the last ~3H^2/(2 m^2) e-folds and has an exponent 4x the Hawking-Moss/stochastic barrier exponent: it misses trapping in the other well and underestimates p_- by many orders of magnitude where p_- is small.",
  "Re-entry: in RD with constant g_*, T_re = T_reheat e^{-n} for a scale that exited n e-folds before the end.",
  "Site percolation p_c = 0.3116 is for uncorrelated sites; the inflationary sign field is correlated (power-law, tilt 2 Lambda_1), so p_c is only a proxy for the network/no-network boundary."
